cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this compendium or the Decision Coprocessor results, please cite the snapshot you used."
title: "Decision Coprocessor: From a Latent Recurrent Sidecar to a Supervised Transition Executor"
abstract: >-
  A two-part empirical study of multi-step decision making with small frozen backbones:
  V1 (latent recurrent sidecar, documented negative), V2 (supervised transition executor,
  mechanism demonstrated; text decomposition refuted under fair representation budgets),
  V2.1 (frozen-checkpoint validation, depth reversal), V2.2 (interface ablations: A1 failure,
  A1-bis zero-training pass, A2 distributional pass, A3 architectural attribution, router bound,
  end-to-end costs), and the confirmation programme C0/C1/C2 (third-audit errata, same-reader
  attribution, three-seed confirmation, blind extrapolation).
authors:
  - family-names: Garrot
    given-names: C.
  - name: "The agent mesh (@ag-1..@ag-5)"
version: "2026-09-26"
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/cgarrot/decision-coprocessor-paper"
keywords:
  - multi-step reasoning
  - latent computation
  - transition executor
  - frozen backbones
  - LoRA
  - pre-registration
  - negative results
